WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.640
Dany: Russia is now in Syria. Vladimir Putin has taken the Crimea.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.110
We seem to have forgotten about it as a nation
already. They're in Donetsk, they're in Luhansk.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:14.690
There's some suspicion they may even go into
some of our NATO-allied countries.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.999
Are we handling Putin correctly?

00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:21.880
Cheney: I don't think so. I think Putin believes
he's got a window here that runs to the end

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.439
of the Obama Administration.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:30.269
We've seen him move on to Crimea as you pointed
out, in the Ukraine, now he's in Syria.

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:35.950
It's as though he is trying to recreate elements
of the old Soviet Empire that came apart back

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.270
in '90 and '91.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:43.710
I think he also has aspirations on the Baltics.
I think he'd like nothing better than to be

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.410
able to put pressure on the Baltics.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:52.910
Not so much directly by military action, but
they all get all of their energy supplies,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:57.539
their gas all comes from Russia. They were
all part of Russia at one time.

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:01.480
The Russians appear to be spending money on
trying to influence the internal politics

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.019
of the Baltics.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:08.200
So if he could stir up enough trouble, I could
see him trying to put pressure on the Baltics

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.880
that they either have to do what he wants
them to do, probably withdraw from NATO, or

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.700
some additional pressures will be brought
to bear on the Baltics.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:24.420
I think that's his real objective. Now will
he pull it off? I don't know and I question

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:30.060
at this point how determined NATO would in
fact be without strong U.S. leadership.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.159
We provide 75% of the funding for NATO and
the defense budgets here in the U.S. have

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:40.030
been cut dramatically. That's provided a rationale
for the Europeans to afford and cut their

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.990
defense budgets as well. So it's worrisome.

